{"id":"9c641a5e-08ca-4d4e-b622-c7be1f1c5423","object":"chat.completion","created":1785026084,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = case['required_symbols']\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        pid = n['parent']\\n        if pid is not None:\\n            children.setdefault(pid, []).append(nid)\\n        if nid not in children:\\n            children[nid] = []\\n    all_ids = set(node_map.keys())\\n    symbol_counts = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n    removed = []\\n    removed_set = set()\\n    # sort by depth descending, then id ascending\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if not n['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        # check retained children\\n        has_retained_child = False\\n        for child_id in children.get(nid, []):\\n            if child_id not in removed_set:\\n                has_retained_child = True\\n                break\\n        if has_retained_child:\\n            continue\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        # check if removing would cause missing required symbol\\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) == 1:\\n            continue\\n        # remove\\n        removed.append(nid)\\n        removed_set.add(nid)\\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts[sym] - 1\\n    retained = sorted(all_ids - removed_set)\\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed,\\n        'retained_node_ids': retained\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task SE-PE-01. The function should process a parse tree (nodes with parent relationships) and decide which nodes to remove (if removable and not required), preserving required symbols. The nodes have fields: id, parent (null for root), symbol, depth, removable, utility. The required_symbols list specifies which symbols must be preserved. The root is always required (id \"root\", symbol \"root\")? The payload has required_symbols array that includes \"root\" and \"s1\". So we must ensure at least one node of each required symbol remains.\n\nThe task description: \"Grammar-guided reduction on a miniature grammar; Perses syntax-guided reduction\". It seems we need to attempt to remove removable nodes while ensuring that for each required symbol, at least one node with that symbol is still present. Also, we cannot remove a node that has retained children (children are nodes whose parent is this node). We must traverse deeper nodes first (depth descending). Use node ID as tie-breaker at equal depth. Return removed_node_ids (list of IDs removed in order of removal) and retained_node_ids (sorted list of IDs that remain after reduction). The root must not be removed (it's not removable anyway). Also, symbol checking: after removal, all required_symbols must have at least one node.\n\nWe need to construct a tree structure from nodes list (each node is dict). Build a map from id to node dict. Also build children list for each parent. Then iterate nodes in order: sort by depth descending, then by ID (alphanumeric? IDs are strings like \"n1\", \"n2\", \"root\", but we should sort lexicographically as string). For each node, check if it is removable (removable=true) and not the root (or any required symbol? Actually the required_symbols list indicates symbols, not node IDs. So we cannot remove a node if its symbol is required and there is no other node with that symbol? Or we must never remove a node that is the only node with that required symbol? The spec: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" It says \"a required symbol\" could mean a node that is the only one representing that required symbol? But more precisely: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" That means before removing a node, we must check that after removal, every required symbol still has at least one node in the tree (i.e., the set of symbols of all retained nodes must include all required_symbols). Also cannot remove a node with retained children (i.e., if any node has parent = this node and is not also removed). But note we are iterating depth-first descending, so children might be removed earlier? Actually deeper nodes are processed first, so children (which are deeper) would have been considered for removal before their parent. So by the time we consider a parent, its children may have already been removed. So we need to check if there are any remaining children (i.e., nodes in the current set with parent=this node and not yet removed). That is, \"retained children\" means children that are still present in the tree at the time of consideration. So we need to maintain a set of deleted IDs, and when checking a node, we look at its children that are not in deleted set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Map node_id -> node dict.\n2. Build children mapping: parent_id -> list of child ids.\n3. Determine initial set of node IDs (all). Also compute set of symbols present (symbol of each node).\n4. Determine which symbols are required: required_symbols list.\n5. Define removed_node_ids list (order of removal).\n6. Get nodes sorted: by depth descending, then by ID ascending (string compare).\n7. For each node in that order:\n   - Skip if node is not removable (removable==false) or node id is \"root\"? Actually root's removable is false, but we can still check removable flag.\n   - Check if node.id is \"root\": should never remove, but root is not removable anyway.\n   - Check if node has retained children: iterate over children of this node (from children map). For each child id, if it is not in removed_node_ids, then there is a retained child -> cannot remove this parent.\n   - Check if removing this node would cause any required symbol to be missing: after removal, the symbol of this node would be lost. So check if the symbol of this node is in required_symbols AND the count of nodes with that symbol in the current remaining set (including this node) is exactly 1. If so, then removing would lose that symbol, so skip. (We need to track symbol counts dynamically? Could compute remaining set before removal and check. Since we are processing in order, we can maintain a symbol count dict that starts with all nodes, then decrement as we remove nodes. When considering removal, if the symbol count for this node's symbol after decrement would be zero and it's required, skip.\n   - If all conditions satisfied, add node.id to removed_node_ids and update symbol counts: decrement for its symbol.\n8. After processing all nodes, retained_node_ids = all node IDs that are not in removed_node_ids, sorted (ascending string order).\n9. Return {\"removed_node_ids\": removed_node_ids, \"retained_node_ids\": retained_node_ids}.\n\nEdge cases: root has parent null; children may have no children (empty list). The symbol counts: initial counts from all nodes. After removal, we need to ensure we still have at least one node for each required symbol. Also, \"a required symbol\" might refer to symbols that appear in required_symbols list. The root symbol is \"root\" which is also in required_symbols. So we cannot remove the only node with symbol \"root\". Since root is not removable, that's fine. But there might be other nodes with symbol \"root\"? Probably only root has that symbol. So no issue.\n\nThe example cases have required_symbols [\"root\", \"s1\"]. So we must keep at least one node with symbol \"s1\" (there are multiple nodes with symbol \"s1\": n1 (depth1, not removable), n4 (depth2, removable), possibly others? In case 0, n1 has symbol s1 and not removable; n4 has symbol s1 and removable; n6 has symbol s0; n5 symbol s2; n2 symbol s2; n3 symbol s0. So s1 is present in n1 (not removable) and n4 (removable). So we can remove n4 if it has no retained children? n4's children? None (depth2, no children listed). So can remove n4. n6 is s0 not required, removable, no children, can be removed. n2 is s2, not required, removable, but has child n4 (which we might remove first). After removing n4, n2 has no retained children (since n4 removed). So n2 can be removed if it doesn't cause loss of required symbols (s2 not required). But check: after removing n2, does any required symbol disappear? s1 still present via n1; root present. So n2 can be removed. n1 is not removable, n3 not removable, root not removable. So final removed: n4, n6, n2 (order depends on depth: deeper first: n4 depth2, n6 depth2, then n2 depth1? Actually n4 and n6 both depth2, tie break by ID: n4 < n6? string compare \"n4\" < \"n6\", so n4 first, then n6, then n2. So removed_node_ids = [\"n4\",\"n6\",\"n2\"]. retained_node_ids = [\"n1\",\"n3\",\"n5\",\"root\"] sorted alphabetically: [\"n1\",\"n3\",\"n5\",\"root\"]. But we need to verify that n5 is not removable (removable: false), so it stays. That matches expected? Not given, but plausible.\n\nNow, the implementation must be a Python function solve(case) that returns a dict with keys \"removed_node_ids\" and \"retained_node_ids\". Should raise ValueError if case is structurally invalid? But the cases are valid, so we can assume valid input.\n\nWe need to include the function definition within the JSON string under \"implementation\". The response must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\". The value is a string containing the Python source code, properly escaped.\n\nLet's write the Python code. We'll use standard library only. We'll parse case payload, which is a dict with \"nodes\" list and \"required_symbols\" list.\n\nImplementation details:\n- Use case (argument) directly as dict.\n- Extract nodes list and required_symbols.\n- Build node_map: {node[\"id\"]: node}.\n- Build children_map: default dict list.\n- For each node, if parent is not None, add child id to parent's list.\n- Initialize all_ids set, symbol_counts dict.\n- Process sorted nodes.\n- Return dict.\n\nMake sure to not mutate case. We'll work on copies or just use references as we only read.\n\nPotential issues: Node IDs are strings, sort as strings (natural order). Depth is integer.\n\nAlso, root node may have parent null, depth 0. Ensure we handle that.\n\nWe need to ensure we check \"retained children\" after removing children that are already removed. Since we process deeper first, when considering a parent, we can check if any child is still present (not in removed). We'll maintain a set \"removed_ids\" that we update as we remove.\n\nLet's produce final code.\n\nWrite as a string within JSON. Need to escape quotes, backslashes, newlines.\n\nI'll write the Python code in a multiline string, then escape for JSON.\n\nI'll produce the response now."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2172,"completion_tokens":2518,"total_tokens":4690,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2079},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":124},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}